post.summary:
Escalate an open / pending case to executive resolution (G-012; `campus.governance.manage`;
Idempotency-Key): opens an `escalation` case (severity at least high) linked to it and emits
`governance_case.escalated`. Returns the new escalation case.

Re-read the figures behind an SLA deviation or KPI review (`campus.governance.manage`;
draft / open only): the SLA snapshot keeps its tickets and refreshes their status, the KPI
snapshot is recomputed against the same targets.

Submit an open case with its proposed outcome for decision (`campus.governance.manage`;
`GOVERNANCE_DECISION`). 422 with every closure rule the outcome breaks; auto-approval closes
the case at once (`governance_case.decided`).

Allocate a batch of students to a session of this lab (`campus.facility.manage`;
`Idempotency-Key`): students already allocated are skipped; 409 when the session would
exceed its capacity; unknown students are 422.

Make a trip ready (`campus.transport.manage`; G-104): a usable vehicle seating the route's
passengers, an active driver of the route valid on the trip date and a complete checklist;
the vehicle becomes `assigned`.

Revise the published timetable (`exam.setup.manage`, reason required, L3-I-008): the
published version becomes `revised` and the next draft version opens with its sittings;
returns the new draft.

Request an approved correction of one paper's final marks (`exam.result.manage`;
`RESULT_CORRECTION`): final marks are revised through `revise_final` and the result is
replaced at the same level (published → `term_result.revised`).

Submit a pending engagement for activation (`people.staff.manage`; If-Match;
`ENGAGEMENT_ACTIVATION`). The staff record must be active (verified). Auto-approval activates it
at once when the start date has come; otherwise it waits for `/activate`.

Change / reassign an active assignment to another position (`people.staff.manage`; If-Match;
`POSITION_ASSIGNMENT`; L3-E-012). The old assignment is superseded (history kept) when the new
one becomes active.

Apply a governed correction with before / after history (`people.staff.manage`; If-Match;
reason required; L3-E-065). Allowed on any record that is not merged (archived history can be
corrected); 422 when nothing changes.

Merge a duplicate onto its canonical record (`people.staff.manage`; If-Match of the duplicate;
L3-E-009). The duplicate's engagements must be closed / cancelled first; its qualifications,
documents and login link move to the canonical record.

Accept the inspected delivery (`resources.procurement.manage`; If-Match; L3-J-054 / 057):
accepted stock lines post `receipt` movements, the order's received quantities rise;
`goods_receipt.accepted`.

Amend quantities / prices of an issued order (`resources.procurement.manage`; If-Match;
reason required; L3-J-045): never below the received quantity; next revision; back to
`draft` for re-approval and re-issue.

Merge a duplicate supplier onto the canonical one (`resources.procurement.manage`; If-Match;
L3-J-035): the duplicate becomes `merged` with `canonicalSupplierId`; refused while it has
open purchase orders or the canonical record is itself merged / inactive.

Hand an approved self-study report off to the accrediting body (H-071;
`services.accreditation.manage`): records the portal reference once, moves the cycle to
`submitted` and emits `accreditation_record.handed_off`.

Submit an open record with its proposed outcome (`services.accreditation.manage`;
`ACCREDITATION_DECISION`): 422 with every rule the outcome breaks; auto-approval closes it at
once (`accreditation_record.decided`).

Roll back to an earlier (superseded) version (`services.report.approve`, step-up; If-Match;
reason required; L3-H-052): the current version is superseded, the earlier one re-published
(`dashboard.rolled_back`). History is never rewritten.

Assemble a submission package from a validated snapshot (`services.report.manage`;
Idempotency-Key): `SUB-…`, linked to the corrected package after a correction; the cycle
moves to `packaged`.

Open a correction of a submitted / acknowledged package (`services.report.manage`; If-Match;
reason required; L3-H-060): the package becomes `corrected`, the cycle returns to
`collecting` for a new snapshot and a corrected package.

StudentProfileUpdate.description:
Body of `PATCH /students/{id}/profile`. Only editable profile attributes are accepted;
identity attributes (names, date of birth, gender) change through identity correction and
are rejected here (unknown member → 4xx). Present = replace; empty string clears.
